    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0750" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg700"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Department of
                                State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-09-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 25, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 239.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I append hereto copy of your telegram of
                    the 21st instant, in relation to the punishment of Miss Melton’s assailants.</p>
                <p>It affords me pleasure to express the gratification here felt at the partial
                    success which your persistent efforts in the case have achieved. You are
                    instructed to convey to the Porte-an expression of the President’s gratification
                    at the evidence of friendly solicitude for the welfare and protection of our
                    citizens in the Ottoman Empire which its action furnishes.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
